1=10 (carry 1)\n\nHundred thousands:1 +5 +1=7\n\nMillions:4 +3=7\n\nTen millions:2 +0=2\n\nHundred millions:8 +2=10. Oh right, so here the hundred millions place adds to 10, which would mean we have a 0 in the hundred millions and carry over 1 to the billions place. But since there are no higher digits, that carried 1 becomes a new digit in the billions place. So the total would be 1,027,704,813?\n\nW
