akes in the carrying over. Let me verify each step once more.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 0+6=6 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens:4+4=8 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds:4+4=8 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands:2+8=10, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen thousands:6+7+1=14 \u2714\ufe0f (4 with carry 1)\n\nHundred thousands:2+8+1=11 \u2714\ufe0f (1 with carry 1)\n\nMillions:5+4+1=10 \u2714\ufe0f (0 with carry 1)\n\nTen millions:2+9+1=12 \u2714\ufe0f (2 with carry 1)\n\nHundred millions:5+7+1=13 \u2714\ufe0f (3 with carry 1)\n\nBillions:1 carried over. So total is 1,317,503,086. Hmm, that seems right. Let me add them using another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers as whole:\n\n522,624,440 + 794,878,646.\n\nLet me break them into parts:\n\n500,000,000 + 700,000,000 = 1,200,000,000\n\n22,000,000 + 94,000,000 = 116,000,000 \u2192 total so far 1,316,000,000\n\n624,440 + 878,646 = ?\n\n600,000 + 800,000 = 1,400,000\n\n24,440 + 78,646 = 103,086\n\nSo 1,400,000 + 103,086 = 1,503,086\n\nAdding that to the previous total: 1,316,000,000 + 1,503,086 = 1,317,503,086. Yep, matches. So the answer is correct.\n</think>\n\n",
