ousands), 9 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nSo when adding the hundred millions place: 4 +8 =12. So that gives 2 in the hundred millions and carryover 1 to the billions place. Since both numbers don't have a digit beyond hundred millions, the carryover becomes the billions digit. So the total sum will have a 1 in the billions place.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right:\n\nOnes:7\n\nTens:0 (with carryover 1)\n\nHundreds:2 (carryover 1)\n\nThousands:0 (carryover1)\n\nTen thousands:0 (carryover1)\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nMillions:7\n\nTen millions:9\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nBillions:1\n\nSo the sum should be 1,297,400,207? Wait, let me check again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me write each digit step by step properly.\n\nLet me align the numbers:\n\n          4 1 7 3 4 4 2 4 0\n        + 8 8 0 0 5 5 9 6 7\n        ---------------------\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n0 +7 =7\n\nTens:4 +6 =10 \u2192 0, carryover 1\n\nHundreds:2 +9 +1 =12 \u2192 2, carryover1\n\nThousands:4 +5 +1 =10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nTen thousands:4 +5 +1 =10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nHundred thousands:3 +0 +1 =4 \u21924, no carryover\n\nMillions:7 +0 =7\n\nTen millions:1 +8 =9\n\nHundred millions:4 +8 =12 \u21922, carryover1\n\nBillions: 0 (since both numbers have no digits beyond hundred millions) plus the carryover 1 \u21921.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\n7 (ones), 0 (tens), 2 (hundreds), 0 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands),4 (hundred thousands),7 (millions),9 (ten millions),2 (hundred millions),1 (billions).\n\nSo the number is 1,297,400,207.\n\nWait, let me confirm with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n417,344,240 + 880,055,967.\n\nLet me break them into parts:\n\n400,000,000 + 17,344,240\n\nplus\n\n800,000,000 + 80,055,967\n\nAdding the millions first: 400M +800M =1,200,000,000\n\nThen 17,344,240 +80,055,967.\n\n17,344,240 +80,055,967:\n\n17,344,240 +80,055,967 = (17,344