ons:6+6=12 \u21922, carry1\n\nBillions:6 (from first number) + 0 (second has no digit here) +1 (carry) =7.\n\nSo the total is 1,241,813,761? Wait, but when I add 633,106,007 and 608,707,754, maybe I should check with another method. Let me add them in parts.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n633,106,007 + 608,707,754\n\nLet's split into millions and the rest.\n\n633 million + 608 million = 1,241 million.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 106,007 + 707,754.\n\n106,007 + 700,000 = 806,007, then +7,754 = 813,761.\n\nSo total is 1,241,000,000 + 813,761 = 1,241,813,761. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be correct.\n</think>\n\n",
