so 39 million) and the second is 98,831,414 (98 million). So adding those two:\n\n39,909,908\n\n+98,831,414\n\n= (39,909,908 + 98,831,414)\n\nLet me add digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:8+4=12 \u21922, carryover1.\n\nTens:0+1=1 +1=2 \u21922.\n\nHundreds:9+4=13 \u21923, carryover1.\n\nThousands:9+1=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:0+3=3 +1=4 \u21924.\n\nHundred thousands:9+8=17 \u21927, carryover1.\n\nMillions:9 (from 39M's millions place? Wait, 39,909,908 is 39,909,908. Breaking down:\n\n39,909,908:\n\nMillions place:9 (since it's 39 million, so the millions digit is 9, the ten millions is 3).\n\nWait, 39,909,908 is 3 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nWait, perhaps I need to write both numbers in their full digit breakdown:\n\nFirst number (39,909,908):\n\nDigits (from right):\n\nPosition 1 (ones):8\n\n2 (tens):0\n\n3 (hundreds):9\n\n4 (thousands):9\n\n5 (ten thousands):0\n\n6 (hundred thousands):9\n\n7 (millions):9\n\n8 (ten millions):3\n\nSecond number (98,831,414):\n\nPosition1:4\n\n2:1\n\n3:4\n\n4:1\n\n5:3\n\n6:8\n\n7:8\n\n8:9\n\nSo adding each column:\n\nPosition1:8+4=12 \u21922, carryover1.\n\nPosition2:0+1=1 +1=2 \u21922.\n\nPosition3:9+4=13 \u21923, carryover1.\n\nPosition4:9+1=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nPosition5:0+3=3 +1=4 \u21924.\n\nPosition6:9+8=17 \u21927, carryover1.\n\nPosition7:9+8=17 +1=18 \u21928, carryover1.\n\nPosition8:3+9=12 +1=13 \u21923, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover1 after the ten millions place, we need to add an extra digit at the beginning: 1.\n\nSo the total of 39,909,908 +98,831,414 is 138,741,322?\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nThe digits after adding would be:\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):3, but with carryover1, so actually, the total would be 1 (carryover) followed by 3, making it 13 in the ten millions place? Wait, maybe I need to track all digits properly.\n\nWait, the positions after adding:\n\nS