e digits together from right to left, the sum should be 314,064,969. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me recount each place step by step to confirm.\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes: 4 +5=9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens:6+0=6 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds:9+0=9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands:6+4=10, so 0 with carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen thousands:2+4=6 +1=7 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred thousands:0+4=4 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nMillions:5+8=13, so 3 with carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen millions:1+9=10 +1=11, so 1 with carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred millions:1+1=2 +1=3 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nYes, that seems right. So the total is 314,064,969. Wait, but let me add them another way to cross-verify. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\n115,620,964 + 198,444,005.\n\nLet me separate the millions:\n\n115,620,964 is 115,000,000 + 620,964\n\n198,444,005 is 198,000,000 + 444,005\n\nAdding the millions parts: 115,000,000 + 198,000,000 = 313,000,000\n\nAdding the smaller parts: 620,964 + 444,005.\n\n620,964 + 444,005:\n\n600,000 + 400,000 = 1,000,000\n\n20,964 + 44,005 = 64,969\n\nSo total of smaller parts: 1,000,000 + 64,969 = 1,064,969\n\nNow add that to the 313,000,000: 313,000,000 + 1,064,969 = 314,064,969. Okay, same result. That's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method. Let's see:\n\n115,620,964\n\n+198,444,005\n\nAdding digit by digit again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4+5=9\n\n6+0=6\n\n9+0=9\n\n6+4=10 (write 0, carry 1)\n\n2+4=6 +1=7\n\n0+4=4\n\n5+8=13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\n1+9=10 +1=11 (write 1, carry 1)\n\n1+1=2 +1=3\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 9,6,9,0,7,4,3,1,3. Wait, but when written as a number, it's 3 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands?), wait no, let me structure it properly.\n\nWait, the digits in order:\n\nThe first digit (leftmost) is the hundred millions place: 3\n\nThen ten millions: 1\n\nMillions: 4\n\nHundred thousands: 0\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:6\n\nOn