0\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):8\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):7\n\nSo when adding each position:\n\nPosition1:6+7=13 \u21923, carryover1\n\nPosition2:8+9+1=18 \u21928, carryover1\n\nPosition3:9+0+1=10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nPosition4:4+5+1=10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nPosition5:9+6+1=16 \u21926, carryover1\n\nPosition6:5+4+1=10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nPosition7:7+0+1=8 \u21928, no carryover?\n\nWait, 7 (from first) +0 (second) +1 (carryover) =8, so no carryover here.\n\nPosition8:6 (first) +8 (second) =14 \u21924, carryover1\n\nPosition9:2 (first) +7 (second) +1 (carryover) =10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nBut since there are no more digits, that carryover1 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\nStarting from the right, the digits are:\n\nPosition1:3\n\nPosition2:8\n\nPosition3:0\n\nPosition4:0\n\nPosition5:6\n\nPosition6:0\n\nPosition7:8\n\nPosition8:4\n\nPosition9:0\n\nPlus the final carryover1, so the total digits are 1 followed by those digits.\n\nSo the sum would be 1,048,060,083?\n\nWait, let me check again step by step:\n\nLet me write the addition vertically:\n\n          2 6 7 5 9 4 9 8 6\n\n        + 7 8 0 4 6 5 0 9 7\n\n        -------------------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:6+7=13 \u21923, carryover1\n\nTens:8+9=17 +1=18 \u21928, carryover1\n\nHundreds:9+0=9 +1=10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nThousands:4+5=9 +1=10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nTen thousands:9+6=15 +1=16 \u21926, carryover1\n\nHundred thousands:5+4=9 +1=10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nMillions:7+0=7 +1=8 \u21928, no carryover\n\nTen millions:6+8=14 \u21924, carryover1\n\nHundred millions:2+7=9 +1=10 \u21920, carryover1\n\nNow, the carryover1 from the hundred millions place becomes the next digit (billions place), so the total is 1 followed by the digits we have.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\n3 (ones),8 (tens),0 (hundreds),0 (thousands),6 (ten thousands),0 (hundred thousands),8 (millions),4 (ten millions),0 (hundred millions), and the 1 in the billions pla