\u21925, carry1.\n\nTen-thousands:7+9=16 +1=17 \u21927, carry1.\n\nHundred-thousands:7+4=11 +1=12 \u21922, carry1.\n\nMillions: the carryover 1.\n\nSo the digits are 1 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands),7 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),0 (hundreds),2 (tens),7 (ones). So 1,275,027. Yes, that's correct.\n\nI think that's right. Let me just do a quick check with approximate numbers. 779,129 is roughly 780,000 and 495,898 is about 500,000. Adding those gives 1,280,000. The exact answer is 1,275,027, which is a bit less, which makes sense because I rounded both numbers up. So that seems plausible. Okay, I think that's the correct sum.\n</think>\n\n",
