s, we write 0 here and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there are no other digits, that carried 1 becomes the millions digit. So the total is 1,068,888.\n\nWait, that seems right. Let me add them numerically without the commas to confirm:\n\n121363 + 947525.\n\nLet me add step by step:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n3 +5 =8 (ones)\n\n6 +2 =8 (tens)\n\n3 +5 =8 (hundreds)\n\n1 (thousands place of first number) +7 (thousands of second) =8 (thousands)\n\n2 (ten thousands of first) +4 (ten thousands of second) =6 (ten thousands)\n\n1 (hundred thousands of first) +9 (hundred thousands of second) =10. So that's 0 with a carryover 1.\n\nAdding the carryover to the millions place gives 1, so the total is 1,068,888.\n\nHmm, yes, that seems correct. I don't think I made a mistake here. Let me try adding them another way to verify.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers as whole numbers:\n\n121,363 + 947,525.\n\nLet me add 121,363 + 900,000 first, which is 1,021,363. Then add the remaining 47,525.\n\n1,021,363 + 47,525.\n\nAdding 40,000 to 1,021,363 gives 1,061,363. Then add 7,525:\n\n1,061,363 +7,525 = 1,068,888. Yep, same result. So that checks out.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 1,068,888.\n</think>\n\n",
