ten thousands is 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: first has 9, second has 1. Plus carryover 1. 9+1+1=11. So hundred thousands is 1, carryover 1 to millions.\n\nSo the total is 1 (millions) 1 (hundred thousands) 3 (ten thousands) 1 (thousands) 5 (hundreds) 9 (tens) 9 (ones). So that's 1,131,599. Wait, but when I first thought I had 1,131,600. Hmm, so maybe I made a mistake in the first calculation. Let me add them using another method to verify.\n\nAlternatively, adding 991,841 + 139,758:\n\nLet me add 991,841 + 100,000 = 1,091,841\n\nThen add 39,758: 1,091,841 + 39,758 = ?\n\n1,091,841 + 30,000 = 1,121,841\n\nThen +9,758: 1,121,841 +9,758 = 1,131,599. Okay, so that matches. So the correct answer is 1,131,599. \n\nWait, but in the initial reasoning steps, when I listed the digits, the hundreds place was 8+7=15, so 5 with a carryover. So hundreds digit is 5. Then thousands place 1+9+1=11, so 1 with carryover. So the thousands digit is 1. Ten thousands: 9+3+1=13, so 3. Hundred thousands:9+1+1=11, so 1. So the digits are indeed 1,131,599. \n\nHmm, so maybe I made a mistake in my first thought when I thought 1,131,600. Probably a miscalculation there. So the correct answer is 1,131,599. Let me confirm once more with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers:\n\n991,841\n\n+139,758\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:1+8=9\n\nTens:4+5=9\n\nHundreds:8+7=15 (write 5, carryover 1)\n\nThousands:1 (from first number) +9 (from second) +1 (carryover) =11 (write 1, carryover 1)\n\nTen thousands:9 +3 +1=13 (write 3, carryover 1)\n\nHundred thousands:9 +1 +1=11 (write 1, carryover 1)\n\nMillions:1 (from carryover)\n\nSo the total is 1,131,599. Yes, that's correct. So the answer should be 1,131,599. I think I confused myself earlier when I thought of 600, but no, the hundreds digit is 5, so the last three digits are 599. Alright, so the final answer is 1,131,599.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 991841 and 139758?  \n# Reasoning: