ds: 9 (from first number) + 3 (from second) = 12, plus 1 is 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands: 6 + 2 = 8, plus 1 is 9. Write 9, no carry.\n\nHundred thousands: 2 + 8 = 10. So write 0 and carry 1 to the millions place. Since there's no higher digits, that 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place. So putting it all together: 1,093,464.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts. Let's see:\n\n269,478 + 800,000 = 1,069,478. Then add the remaining 23,986 (since 823,986 - 800,000 = 23,986). \n\nAdding 1,069,478 + 23,986:\n\n1,069,478 + 20,000 = 1,089,478\n\nThen +3,986: 1,089,478 + 3,000 = 1,092,478; then +986 = 1,093,464. Okay, same result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another approach. Let me add the numbers digit by digit again to confirm.\n\nFirst number: 269,478\n\nSecond number: 823,986\n\nAdding each digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 8 +6 =14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\nTens:7+8=15 +1=16 \u21926, carry1\n\nHundreds:4+9=13 +1=14 \u21924, carry1\n\nThousands:9+3=12 +1=13 \u21923, carry1\n\nTen thousands:6+2=8 +1=9 \u21929, no carry\n\nHundred thousands:2+8=10 \u21920, carry1\n\nThen the carried 1 goes to the millions place, so total is 1,093,464. Yep, that's consistent. So the answer should be 1,093,464.\n</think>\n\n",
