      "index": 0,
      "text": "\nOkay, let's tackle this addition problem step by step. The question is asking for the sum of 317,699 and 783,724. Hmm, I need to add these two numbers together. Let me write them down to visualize better.\n\nFirst, I'll align the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n  317699\n+783724\n--------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 9 and 4. Adding those gives 13. Wait, so I write down 3 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 9 and 2, plus the carried-over 1. That's 9 + 2 + 1 = 12. So I put 2 in the tens place and carry over another 1.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 6 and 7. Adding them with the carry-over: 6 + 7 = 13, plus 1 makes 14. So I write 4 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 again.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits here are 7 and 3. Adding those gives 10, plus the carried 1 equals 11. So I write 1 in the thousands place and carry over 1.\n\nNext up is the ten-thousands place. The digits are 1 and 8. Adding them with the carry-over: 1 + 8 = 9, plus 1 makes 10. So I put 0 here and carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred-thousands place. The digits are 3 and 7. Adding them plus the carried-over 1: 3 + 7 = 10, plus 1 is 11. So I write 1 in the hundred-thousands place and another 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 1,101,423. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make any mistakes in the carrying over. Starting from the right again:\n\nOnes: 9+4=13 \u2714\ufe0f\nTens: 9+2+1=12 \u2714\ufe0f\nHundreds:6+7+1=14 \u2714\ufe0f\nThousands:7+3+1=11 \u2714\ufe0f\nTen-thousands:1+8+1=10 \u2714\ufe0f\nHundred-thousands:3+7+1=11 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nYes, that seems right. So the final answer should be 1,101,423.\n</think>\n\n",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": "####",
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
  ],
