n- Hundreds:2\n- Tens:1\n- Ones:7\n\nWait, so when adding the hundreds place: first number has 5, second has 2. So 5+2=7, plus the carried 1 makes 8. That's correct. \n\nThousands place: first number's thousands digit is 8, second is 1. 8+1=9. Correct. \n\nTen-thousands place: 7 +7=14. So 4 with a carryover. \n\nHundred thousands: 2+5=7 plus the 1 carried over becomes 8. \n\nSo the total is 849,802. Hmm, but let me add them another way to verify. Maybe using another method like expanded form.\n\n278,585 can be written as 200,000 + 70,000 + 8,000 + 500 + 80 +5\n\n571,217 is 500,000 +70,000 +1,000 +200 +10 +7\n\nAdding each part:\n\n200,000 +500,000 =700,000\n\n70,000 +70,000=140,000 \u2192 total so far 840,000\n\n8,000 +1,000=9,000 \u2192 849,000\n\n500 +200=700 \u2192 849,700\n\n80 +10=90 \u2192 849,790\n\n5+7=12 \u2192 849,790 +12=849,802. \n\nOkay, that matches. So the answer should be correct. I think that's solid. Maybe I can also use a calculator check, but since I can't here, the two methods align. So I'm confident the sum is 849,802.\n</think>\n\n",
