 \n6  \n\nNow, adding all together:\n\nStart with 800,000 + 100,000 = 900,000  \nThen add 60,000 +5,000 =65,000 \u2192 total so far 965,000  \nNext, 4,000 +900 =4,900 \u2192 total 969,900  \nThen 800 +80 =880 \u2192 total 970,780  \nThen 30 +6 =36 \u2192 total 970,816  \nFinally, the 1 \u2192 970,817. \n\nAh! I see, in my previous breakdown calculation I forgot to add the final 1 from the first number. So the correct total is 970,817. That matches the first method. So my initial calculation was right, and the second method had a step missed. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 970,817. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I should do the addition vertically again to confirm. Let's try that:\n\n```\n   864831\n+ 105986\n---------\n```\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 1 +6 =7  \nTens: 3 +8 =11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1  \nHundreds: 8 +9 +1 =18 \u2192 write 8, carryover 1  \nThousands: 4 +5 +1 =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1  \nTen-thousands: 6 +0 +1 =7  \nHundred-thousands: 8 +1 =9  \n\nSo writing all together: 9 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 7 (ones). So 970,817. \n\nYes, that's consistent. So the answer is correct. I think my confusion came from a miscalculation in the breakdown method earlier, but after correcting that, both methods agree. \n\nTherefore, the sum of 864,831 and 105,986 is indeed 970,817.\n</think>\n\n",
