cond has 1. Adding those gives 7 +1 =8, plus the carried over 1 makes it 9. So the hundred thousands place is 9.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 935,777. Wait, let me check again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nWait, let me re-add each column carefully:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 5 +2 =7 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens:9 +8 =17. Write 7, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds:1 +5 =6, plus the carried 1 makes 7 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands:2 +3 =5 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen thousands:4 +9 =13. Write 3, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred thousands:7 +1 =8 plus 1 carried is 9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nSo combining all digits: 9 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 7 (ones). So 935,777. That seems right. Let me confirm with another method, maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, 742,195 + 193,582. Let's break them into smaller parts:\n\n742,195 + 100,000 = 842,195\n\nThen add 93,582: 842,195 +93,582.\n\nAdding 842,195 +90,000 = 932,195\n\nThen add 3,582: 932,195 +3,582 = 935,777. Yep, same result. Okay, that checks out. So the answer should be 935,777.\n</think>\n\n",
