ryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 2 = 11, plus the 1 carried over is 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 2 + 5 = 7, plus 1 is 8. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands: 1 + 2 = 3. Write 3.\n\nHundred-thousands: 2 + 9 = 11. Wait, here, the digits in the hundred-thousands place are 2 (from first number) and 9 (from second number). So 2 + 9 = 11. Since there's no higher place, this would be 11, so we write 1 in the hundred-thousands place and carryover 1 to the millions place. But since there's no millions place in the original numbers, that 1 becomes a new digit at the front.\n\nSo putting all together, the digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:7, Tens:0, Hundreds:2, Thousands:8, Ten-thousands:3, Hundred-thousands:1, and then the carried-over 1 in the millions place.\n\nSo the total sum is 1 (millions), 1 (hundred-thousands), 3 (ten-thousands), 8 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 7 (ones). So that's 1,138,207?\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait, the hundred-thousands place addition was 2 +9 =11, so that gives 1 in the hundred-thousands and carryover 1 to millions. So the millions place is 1. So the total is 1,138,207?\n\nWait, let me add the numbers another way to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, adding 212,963 + 925,244.\n\nLet me break them into parts:\n\n212,963 + 900,000 = 1,112,963\n\nThen add the remaining 25,244:\n\n1,112,963 + 25,244 = ?\n\n1,112,963 + 20,000 = 1,132,963\n\nThen +5,244: 1,132,963 +5,000 = 1,137,963; then +244 = 1,138,207. Okay, that matches.\n\nSo the answer should be 1,138,207.\n\nWait, but in the initial digit-by-digit breakdown, let me check again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:3+4=7\n\nTens:6+4=10 \u2192 0 carry 1\n\nHundreds:9+2=11 +1=12 \u2192 2 carry 1\n\nThousands:2+5=7 +1=8 \u2192 8, no carry\n\nTen-thousands:1+2=3\n\nHundred-thousands:2+9=11 \u2192 1 and carry 1.\n\nThen the carryover 1 becomes the millions place. So the digits are:\n\nMillions:1, Hundred-thousands:1, Ten-thousands:3, thousands:8, hundreds:2, tens:0, ones:7 \u219