  \n= ?\n\nAdding the ones: 1+0=1  \nTens: 9+4=13 (carry 1)  \nHundreds:5+8+1=14 (carry 1)  \nThousands:1+7+1=9 (no carry)  \nTen-thousands:3+7=10 (carry 1)  \nHundred-thousands:9+7+1=17 (carry 1)  \nMillions: the carried 1.\n\nYes, that gives 1,709,431. I think that's correct. Let me confirm with another method. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts:\n\n931,591 can be 900,000 + 31,591  \n777,840 is 700,000 + 77,840  \n\nAdding the hundreds thousands: 900k + 700k = 1,600,000  \nThen the remaining parts: 31,591 + 77,840. Let's add those:\n\n31,591 + 77,840  \n= (30,000 + 1,591) + (70,000 + 7,840)  \n= 100,000 + (1,591 +7,840)  \nWait, no, that's not right. Let me just add them straight:\n\n31,591  \n+77,840  \n= ?\n\nAdding ones:1+0=1  \nTens:9+4=13 (carry 1)  \nHundreds:5+8+1=14 (carry 1)  \nThousands:1+7+1=9  \nTen-thousands:3+7=10 (carry 1)  \nSo that gives 109,431. Wait, so 31,591 +77,840 = 109,431?\n\nWait, 31,591 + 70,000 is 101,591, then adding 7,840 more: 101,591 +7,840 = 109,431. Yes. \n\nSo total sum is 1,600,000 + 109,431 = 1,709,431. That matches my previous result. Okay, so I think that's correct. Therefore, the answer should be 1,709,431.\n</think>\n\n",
