housands: 3 (from first number) + 5 (from second) = 8, plus the 1 carried over is 9. So 9, no carry. \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen-thousands: 4 + 1 = 5. \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred-thousands: 6 + 9 = 15. So write 5 and carry 1. Then the millions place is that 1. \n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (millions), 5 (hundred-thousands), 5 (ten-thousands), 9 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 3 (ones). So the total is 1,559,033?\n\nWait, let me add them numerically another way to confirm. \n\n643,873 + 915,160. Let's break it down:\n\n600,000 + 900,000 = 1,500,000\n\n43,000 + 15,000 = 58,000 \u2192 total so far 1,558,000\n\n873 + 160 = 1,033 \u2192 adding that gives 1,558,000 + 1,033 = 1,559,033. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be 1,559,033.\n</think>\n\n",
