 the hundred thousands, then the rest as before.\n\nLet me check that again. Let's write it step by step properly:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 + 9 = 11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 2 + 1 + 1 (carryover) = 4 \u2192 no carryover.\n\nHundreds: 1 + 6 = 7.\n\nThousands: 6 + 3 = 9.\n\nTen thousands: 1 + 2 = 3.\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 6 = 13 \u2192 write 3, carryover 1 to the millions place.\n\nSo the millions place gets the 1. So putting all together, the sum is 1,339,741?\n\nWait, let me verify that. Let me add the numbers again step by step:\n\n716,122\n\n+623,619\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 + 9 = 11 \u2192 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 2 + 1 = 3 + 1 = 4 \u2192 4.\n\nHundreds: 1 + 6 = 7.\n\nThousands: 6 + 3 = 9.\n\nTen thousands: 1 + 2 = 3.\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 6 = 13 \u2192 so 3 with a carryover 1.\n\nAdding the carryover to the millions place: 1.\n\nSo the total is 1,339,741. Let me check with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, 716,122 + 600,000 is 1,316,122. Then add 23,619 more. 1,316,122 + 23,619 = ?\n\n1,316,122 + 20,000 = 1,336,122\n\nThen +3,619: 1,336,122 + 3,000 = 1,339,122; then +619 = 1,339,741. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be 1,339,741.\n</think>\n\n",
