r: 550,091\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n- Hundred thousands: 5\n\n- Ten thousands: 5\n\n- Thousands: 0\n\n- Hundreds: 0\n\n- Tens: 9\n\n- Ones: 1\n\nSecond number: 323,377\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n- Hundred thousands: 3\n\n- Ten thousands: 2\n\n- Thousands: 3\n\n- Hundreds: 3\n\n- Tens: 7\n\n- Ones:7\n\nWait, so when adding, let's align each place correctly:\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\nOnes: 1 +7 =8\n\nTens:9 +7=16 (carryover 1)\n\nHundreds:0 +3 =3, plus the carryover 1 makes 4.\n\nThousands place: 0 (from first number) +3 (from second) =3\n\nTen thousands place:5 (from first) +2 (from second) =7\n\nHundred thousands place:5 +3 =8\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum should be 873,468?\n\nWait, let me add them numerically without the commas to be precise:\n\n550091\n\n+323377\n\nLet's add digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1st digit (ones):1+7=8\n\n2nd digit (tens):9+7=16 \u2192 write 6, carryover 1\n\n3rd digit (hundreds):0+3=3 +1=4\n\n4th digit (thousands):0+3=3\n\n5th digit (ten thousands):5+2=7\n\n6th digit (hundred thousands):5+3=8\n\nSo combining all digits: 8 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 8 (ones). So 873,468.\n\nWait, but when I add 550,091 and 323,377, let me check with another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, adding 550,091 + 323,377:\n\n550,091 + 300,000 = 850,091\n\nThen add 23,377: 850,091 +23,377 = ?\n\n850,091 +20,000 = 870,091\n\n870,091 +3,377 = 873,468. Yep, same result. So that seems correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 873,468.\n</think>\n\n",
