rom first number) and 5 (from second). 1+5=6 +1=7. Correct.\n\nHundred-thousands: 9 +2 =11. So yes, that gives 11 in the hundred-thousands and millions place. So combining all, it's 1,170,742. Hmm, but let me add them another way to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking the numbers into parts:\n\n913,914 + 256,828.\n\nLet me add the hundreds first: 913,914 is 900,000 + 13,914. 256,828 is 200,000 + 56,828.\n\nAdding the hundreds thousands: 900k + 200k = 1,100,000.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 13,914 +56,828. Let's compute that:\n\n13,914 +56,828:\n\n13,000 +56,000 =69,000.\n\n914 +828 = 1,742.\n\nSo total of those parts: 69,000 +1,742 =70,742.\n\nAdding to the 1,100,000 gives 1,170,742. Okay, same result. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method: 913,914 +256,828.\n\nLet me add 913,914 + 200,000 first: that's 1,113,914.\n\nThen add 56,828: 1,113,914 +56,828.\n\nAdding 50,000 to 1,113,914 gives 1,163,914.\n\nThen 6,828 more: 1,163,914 +6,828 = 1,170,742. Yep, same answer.\n\nHmm, so I think that's correct. The final sum should be 1,170,742.\n</think>\n\n",
