tarting over with the carry-over steps properly:\n\nWait, let me retrace each step carefully to avoid mistakes.\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes: 5 +8=13 \u2192 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 5 +2 +1=8 \u2192 no carryover.\n\nHundreds:6+2=8 \u2192 no carryover.\n\nThousands:7+4=11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands:9+7 +1 (carryover) =17 \u2192 write 7, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands:4+6 +1 (carryover) =11 \u2192 here, since there are no more digits, we have to add that 11. But since it's the hundred-thousands place, 11 would mean 1 in the hundred-thousands and 1 in the millions place. So the total would be 1 (million) 1 (hundred thousand), then the rest.\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nMillions place: 1\n\nHundred-thousands:1\n\nTen-thousands:7\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:8\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:3\n\nSo the total is 1,171,883?\n\nWait, let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, break down the numbers:\n\n497,655 + 674,228.\n\nLet me add 497,655 + 600,000 = 1,097,655.\n\nThen add 74,228: 1,097,655 +74,228.\n\n1,097,655 +70,000 = 1,167,655.\n\nThen +4,228: 1,167,655 +4,228 = 1,171,883. Okay, same result. So that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add them digit by digit again:\n\nLet me write it out vertically again:\n\n      497655\n    +674228\n    ---------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:5+8=13 \u2192 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens:5+2=7, plus 1 is 8. So 8, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:6+2=8. So 8.\n\nThousands:7+4=11 \u2192 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands:9+7=16, plus 1 is 17 \u2192 7, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands:4+6=10, plus 1 is 11 \u2192 1, carryover 1. But since there are no more digits, that carryover 1 becomes a new digit at the front. So the total is 1,171,883. Yes, that matches.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 1,171,883.\n</think>\n\n",
      "logprobs": null,
