Tens:8+0=8  \nHundreds:8+4=12 (carry 1)  \nThousands:9+6+1=16 (carry 1)  \nTen-thousands:1+9+1=11 (carry 1)  \nHundred-thousands:9+4+1=14 (carry 1)  \nMillions: the carried 1.\n\nSo yes, that gives 1,416,288. I think that's correct. Maybe another way to verify is to approximate. 900,000 + 500,000 is 1,400,000. The actual numbers are a bit more, so 1,416,288 makes sense. Okay, confident with that answer.\n</think>\n\n",
