, let me verify by adding the numbers another way. Maybe breaking them into parts:\n\n625,231 + 780,357\n\nLet's split them into thousands and the rest:\n\n625,231 = 600,000 + 25,000 + 231\n\n780,357 = 700,000 + 80,000 + 357\n\nAdding the large chunks first:\n\n600,000 + 700,000 = 1,300,000\n\n25,000 + 80,000 = 105,000\n\n231 + 357 = 588\n\nNow add those results together:\n\n1,300,000 + 105,000 = 1,405,000\n\nThen add 588: 1,405,000 + 588 = 1,405,588\n\nOkay, that matches my previous result. So the sum is indeed 1,405,588. I think that's correct. Let me just do a quick check using another method, maybe rounding.\n\nRound 625,231 to the nearest thousand: 625,000\n\nRound 780,357 to the nearest thousand: 780,000\n\nAdding those gives 625,000 + 780,000 = 1,405,000. The actual sum should be a bit more because we rounded down both numbers. Since the original numbers were 231 and 357 over their rounded values, the total extra is 231 + 357 = 588. So adding that to 1,405,000 gives exactly 1,405,588. Perfect, that's consistent.\n\nI think I'm confident now. The answer should be 1,405,588.\n</think>\n\n",
