,352 +50 = 1,284,402\n\nWait, but then adding 8 more? Wait, maybe this method is getting confusing. Alternatively, perhaps adding the two numbers as whole:\n\n943,652\n\n+340,758\n\nLet me add the thousands first. 943,652 is 943 thousands and 652. 340,758 is 340 thousands and 758. Adding the thousands: 943 + 340 = 1,283 thousands. Then the remaining parts: 652 +758 = 1,410. So total is 1,283,000 + 1,410 = 1,284,410. Okay, that matches the first method. So that's correct.\n\nI think that's right. So the final answer should be 1,284,410.\n</think>\n\n",
