step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 0 +3 =3  \nTens:0+4=4  \nHundreds:8+8=16, so 6 with carryover 1  \nThousands:3 (from first number) +2 (from second) =5, plus 1 is 6  \nTen thousands:6 +5=11, so 1 and carryover 1  \nHundred thousands:5+8=13 +1=14, so 4 and carryover 1  \nMillions: 1. \n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (million), 4 (hundred thousand), 1 (ten thousand), 6 (thousand), 6 (hundred), 4 (ten), 3 (one). So 1,416,643. Yep, that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
