ousands: 7 + 8 =15 \u21925, carryover 1\nHundred-thousands:1 +1 =2 +1=3 \u21923\n\nSo combining all the digits: 3 (hundred-thousands), 5 (ten-thousands), 4 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 1 (ones). So the total is 354,321. Wait, but let me check if the positions are correct. Let me write the numbers aligned properly:\n\n      1 7 4 1 6 2\n    +1 8 0 1 5 9\n    ---------------\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\n2 +9 =11 \u2192 1, carryover 1\n6 +5 =11 +1=12 \u21922, carryover1\n1 +1=2 +1=3 \u21923\n4 +0=4 \u21924\n7 +8=15 \u21925, carryover1\n1 +1=2 +1=3 \u21923\n\nYes, so the sum is 354,321. Hmm, but let me add them another way to confirm. Maybe breaking them into parts.\n\n174,162 + 180,159. Let's split into 174,000 + 162 and 180,000 + 159. Adding the thousands first: 174,000 + 180,000 = 354,000. Then the remaining parts: 162 + 159 = 321. So total is 354,000 + 321 = 354,321. That matches. Okay, so the answer should be 354,321.\n</think>\n\n",
