 +1 =16. So 6 with a carryover 1. That gives the 1 in the millions. So the total is 1,619,640. Hmm, but let me add them another way to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers as whole numbers:\n\n971,028 + 648,612. Let's break them down:\n\n900,000 + 600,000 = 1,500,000\n\n70,000 + 40,000 = 110,000 \u2192 total so far 1,610,000\n\n1,000 + 8,000 = 9,000 \u2192 1,619,000\n\n28 + 612 = 640 \u2192 total 1,619,640. Okay, that matches. So I think that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
