perly:\n\n  489665\n+273202\n--------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:5+2=7\n\nTens:6+0=6\n\nHundreds:6+2=8\n\nThousands:9+3=12 (carryover 1)\n\nTen thousands:8+7=15 +1=16 (carryover 1)\n\nHundred thousands:4+2=6 +1=7\n\nSo yes, the digits are 7 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 7 (ones). So 762,867.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers in a different way, like adding 489,665 + 200,000 first, then adding the remaining 73,202?\n\nWait, 489,665 + 200,000 = 689,665. Then adding 73,202:\n\n689,665 +70,000 =759,665\n\n759,665 +3,202 =762,867. Yep, same result.\n\nAlright, so I think that's correct. The answer should be 762,867.\n</think>\n\n",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": "####",
      "prompt_logprobs": null
