+6=9\n\nThousands:5 (from first number) +6 (from second) =11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:0 +4 =4, plus the carryover 1 makes 5.\n\nHundred thousands:4 +3 =7.\n\nSo combining all digits: 7 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 5 (ones). So the total is 751,975.\n\nWait, but let me confirm by adding another way. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\n405,361 can be 400,000 + 5,000 + 300 + 60 +1\n\n346,614 is 300,000 +40,000 +6,000 +600 +10 +4\n\nAdding each part:\n\n400k +300k =700k\n\n5k +40k =45k (so total so far 745k)\n\n6k +6k =12k (total 745k +12k =757k?)\n\nWait, maybe this approach is confusing. Alternatively, adding the numbers step by step:\n\n405,361 + 346,614.\n\nLet me add 400,000 + 300,000 =700,000.\n\nThen 5,000 +40,000 =45,000 \u2192 total 745,000.\n\nThen 300 +6,000 =6,300 \u2192 total 745,000 +6,300 =751,300.\n\nThen 60 +600 =660 \u2192 751,300 +660 =751,960.\n\nThen 1 +10 +4 =15 \u2192 751,960 +15 =751,975. Okay, same result. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method. Let me check with calculator steps:\n\n405361 + 346614.\n\nAdding the numbers:\n\nStart from the right:\n\nOnes:1+4=5\n\nTens:6+1=7\n\nHundreds:3+6=9\n\nThousands:5+6=11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:0+4=4 plus 1 is 5.\n\nHundred thousands:4+3=7.\n\nSo the sum is 751,975. That's consistent. I think that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
