 \u2714\ufe0f (then carryover)\nTen-thousands:7+5+1=13 \u2714\ufe0f\nHundred-thousands:3+8+1=12 \u2714\ufe0f\nAnd the final carryover gives the 1 in millions place. So combining all the digits: 1 (million), 2 (hundred thousand), 3 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 8 (hundred), 5 (ten), 6 (one). Yep, that's 1,235,856. I think that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
